{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774716,"nonce":"vjGdhQJrjsFAmbNB6IgUwqUBZjA=","title":"feat(dashboard): run bars encode duration in height + refined styling","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #27 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/runbars-duration` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-18T11:22:44Z · Merged: 2026-07-18T11:47:20Z\n\nFollow-up to #26. The pass/fail strip read flat and ugly — every bar was full height, so it carried only *outcome*, not how long each run took. This restores the organic look of the earlier `Sparkline` (found in git history — varied heights, rounded, colored) and drives bar **height from real run duration**.\n\n- `RunSummaryDto.duration_ms` = `updated_at - created_at` (the `runs` table already tracks `updated_at`; no migration).\n- Threaded through `RunSummary` (+ `#[derive(Default)]` on `Timestamp`), and both `list_runs` / `list_runs_for_tenant` in Postgres and the testkit fake.\n- Regenerated `openapi.json` + TS client. `scarab-server` dashboard + route-coverage tests green.\n\n- **Height = duration**, `sqrt`-scaled against the strip's peak so one long run doesn't flatten the rest, with a floor so short runs still read.\n- Rounded tops, taller strip, status colours (green pass / red fail / amber gate / muted in-flight).\n\n![dashboard](docs/assets/screenshots/dashboard-light.jpg)\n\nFor an in-flight run `duration_ms` is elapsed-to-last-transition (the fake reports 0 — it has no clock at transition time; real Postgres is accurate).\n\nCloses (git-bug): `7107fcb`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}